CHAPTER III
RIGHTS OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN
FROM ACTS OF VIOLENCE
Article 4
Women and children victims of acts of violence receive the following rights:
a. the right to have their dignity and worth as human beings respected; b. the right to health and psychological services for the suffering experienced by victims;
c. the right to legal assistance;
d. the right to obtain information;
e. the right to confidential handling;
f. the right to social rehabilitation;
g. the right to complaint handling;
h. the right of victims and their families to obtain facilitation in the judicial process; and
i. guarantee of rights related to status as members of the family and society.

Article 5
Child victims of acts of violence, in addition to obtaining the rights as referred to in article 4, also obtain special rights as follows: a. the right to survival, growth and development;
b. the right to basic service needs;
c. the right to equal protection; and
d. the right to obtain freedom;

CHAPTER II
PRINCIPLES AND OBJECTIVES
Article 2
The Implementation and Protection of Women and Children from victims of acts of violence is carried out based on the principles of:
a. humanity;
b. respect for the rights of victims;
c. justice and gender equality;
d. protection;
e. non-discrimination; and
f. best interests of victims.

REGENT OF SORONG,

Considering : a. that violence against women and children is an act that violates the rights and dignity of women and children as human beings;
b. that the implementation of prevention and protection of women and children as victims of violence in Sorong Regency has not been carried out optimally;
c. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a and letter b, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation on the Protection of Women and Children from Acts of Violence;

In View of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
